title: Filters
description: Stack up to four filters on a clip, from Blur and Pixelate to Sepia and Vignette, set how strong each one is, and animate them.
---

import { Steps } from '@astrojs/starlight/components';
import AtAGlance from '@components/AtAGlance.astro';

Filters change how a clip looks: soften it, break it into blocks, turn it black and white, darken its corners. A clip can carry up to four at once, and any clip that draws can have them, text, shapes and graphics included.

<AtAGlance
  menu="Edit ▸ Paste Attributes"
  keys="⌥⌘V"
  where="Clip tab ▸ Picture ▸ Filters"
  tools={['set_video', 'set_action_end', 'paste_attributes']}
/>

## Add a filter

<Steps>

1. Select the clip and open the **Clip** tab's [**Picture**](/canvas/picture-tab/) sub-tab.

2. Open the **Filters** section. On a clip with none it reads "No filters on this clip."

3. Choose **Add Filter**. A Blur at 50 % joins the end of the stack.

4. Pick the filter you want in the row's popup, and set its **Amount**.

</Steps>
